---
// Reading about Helico goes to the docs site; looking at the code goes to GitHub.
const docs = 'https://docs.helico.site/docs'
const record = `${docs}/evidence`
const cards = [
	{ label: 'Never held', title: 'Your funds stay in your wallet.', copy: 'The contract moves them for one step, and proves it kept none before that step ends.' },
	{ label: 'Never outside your rules', title: 'Break a rule and the move is refused.', copy: 'The contract checks every rule itself. 291 assertions run against it on every change.' },
	{ label: 'Nothing hidden', title: 'All of the code is public.', copy: 'Five contracts are deployed on Arbitrum One with their source verified. Twelve automated reviewers went over them, which is not a professional audit.' },
]
---

<section class="wrap" id="verified" aria-labelledby="verified-title">
	<div class="section-card center" data-reveal>
		<span class="eyebrow">Helico</span>
		<h2 class="headline" id="verified-title">Your Money Stays Yours</h2>
		<p class="lede">It can move your funds. It can never keep them.</p>
		<div class="cards" style="text-align:left">
			{cards.map((c) => (
				<div class="card">
					<span class="label">{c.label}</span>
					<h3>{c.title}</h3>
					<p>{c.copy}</p>
				</div>
			))}
		</div>

		<div class="split">
			<div>
				<h3>80% put to work, because the rule said 80%.</h3>
				<p>In a rehearsal on a copy of the real market, 50,000 USDC was funded and 40,000 went into Aave v3 — the share the rules asked for, to the unit — leaving a 10,000 buffer. The agent ended holding none of it. A rehearsal, not the live network.</p>
			</div>
			<a class="btn btn--secondary" href={record}>See the Record</a>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	.cards {
		margin-top: 2rem;
	}
</style>
